  "question": {
    "text": "The sum of the series $\\frac{1}{1.2}-\\frac{1}{2.3}+\\frac{1}{3.4} \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots .$. up to $\\infty$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "IZnA5",
      "text": "\n$\\log _e\\left(\\frac{4}{e}\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "xSP6V",
      "text": "\n$2 \\log _e 2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OLF8u",
      "text": "\n$\\log _{\\mathrm{e}} 2-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jaTFY",
      "text": "\n$\\log _{\\mathrm{e}} 2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{1}{1.2}-\\frac{1}{2.3}+\\frac{1}{3.4} \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots\\infty$\nLet $T_n=\\frac{1}{n(n+1)}=\\left(\\frac{1}{n}-\\frac{1}{n+1}\\right)$\n$\\mathrm{S}=\\mathrm{T}_1-\\mathrm{T}_2+\\mathrm{T}_3-\\mathrm{T}_4+\\mathrm{T}_5 \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots$\n$=\\left(\\frac{1}{1}-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{5}\\right) \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots$.\n$=1-2\\left[\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{5} \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots \\infty\\right]$\n$=1-2[-\\log (1+1)+1]=2 \\log 2-1=\\log \\left(\\frac{4}{e}\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
